According to `GENERAL_AI_TRAINING_KNOWLEDGE.md` (General AI Training Knowledge & Systems Engineering Reference > 3. General Dataset Formats > 3.12 MosaicML MDS / streaming formats):

Streaming dataset systems commonly divide datasets into binary shards
plus metadata/index information.

Typical goals:

- deterministic shuffling;
- streaming;
- local caching;
- worker resumption;
- distributed ingestion.

They can be excellent when the training framework and infrastructure are
designed around streaming.

